import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.List;

public class Main {
&#x20;   public static List\<String> alphabetize(List\<String> strings) {
&#x20;       List\<String> sorted = new ArrayList<>(strings);
&#x20;       sorted.sort(String.CASE_INSENSITIVE_ORDER);
&#x20;       return sorted;
&#x20;   }

&#x20;   public static void main(String[] args) {
&#x20;       List\<String> words = Arrays.asList("banana", "Apple", "cherry", "avocado");

&#x20;       System.out.println(alphabetize(words));
&#x20;       // Output: [Apple, avocado, banana, cherry]
&#x20;   }
}

This sorts alphabetically **ignoring capitalization** and returns a new list, leaving the original unchanged.

Here are two clean ways to sort a list of strings in alphabetical order in Java: using the modern `List.sort()` method with `Comparator.naturalOrder()`, and using `Collections.sort()`.

### Method 1: Using `List.sort()` (Java 8+)

Java
```
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.Comparator;
import java.util.List;

public class AlphabeticalSort {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Create a list of strings
        List<String> fruits = new ArrayList<>();
        fruits.add("Banana");
        fruits.add("Apple");
        fruits.add("Dragonfruit");
        fruits.add("Cherry");

        // Sort in alphabetical order (case-sensitive)
        fruits.sort(Comparator.naturalOrder());

        // Display the sorted list
        System.out.println("Alphabetical Order: " + fruits);
    }
}

```

### Method 2: Case-Insensitive Sorting

By default, uppercase letters come before lowercase letters in Java (e.g., `"banana"` comes after `"Apple"`). To sort alphabetically regardless of letter casing, use `String.CASE_INSENSITIVE_ORDER`:

Java
```
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class CaseInsensitiveSort {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<String> names = new ArrayList<>();
        names.add("banana");
        names.add("Apple");
        names.add("cherry");
        names.add("Date");

        // Sort ignoring capital vs. lowercase letters
        names.sort(String.CASE_INSENSITIVE_ORDER);

        System.out.println("Case-Insensitive Order: " + names);
    }
}

```

### Key Options Breakdown

| **Approach**               | **Code Method**                            | **Behavior**                                                |
| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Standard Natural Order** | `list.sort(Comparator.naturalOrder())`     | Standard ASCII alphabetical sort (uppercase letters first). |
| **Case-Insensitive**       | `list.sort(String.CASE_INSENSITIVE_ORDER)` | True alphabetical order, ignoring capitalization.           |
| **Reverse Alphabetical**   | `list.sort(Comparator.reverseOrder())`     | Sorts from Z to A.                                          |
